<div class="container">

<header>
    <h1>Global Airbnb Market Comparison</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">A comprehensive cross-city analysis of Airbnb listings across 7 major cities, examining pricing dynamics, room-type distribution, host concentration, and guest engagement patterns.</p>
    <div class="meta">
        <strong>Report Date:</strong> April 2026 &nbsp;|&nbsp;
        <strong>Data Source:</strong> Inside Airbnb (scraped March 2026) &nbsp;|&nbsp;
        <strong>Total Listings:</strong> 50,000
    </div>
</header>

<div class="toc">
    <h2>Table of Contents</h2>
    <div class="toc-grid">
        <a href="#overview"><span>01</span> Global Market Overview</a>
        <a href="#pricing"><span>02</span> Pricing Dynamics Across Cities</a>
        <a href="#supply"><span>03</span> Supply Structure & Host Concentration</a>
        <a href="#demand"><span>04</span> Guest Demand & Review Activity</a>
        <a href="#availability"><span>05</span> Availability & Booking Constraints</a>
        <a href="#takeaways"><span>06</span> Key Takeaways & Strategic Implications</a>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="exec-summary">
    <h2>Executive Summary</h2>
    <ol>
        <li><strong>Bangkok commands the highest median prices ($1,400/night)</strong>, driven by a concentration of high-end entire-home listings and a 60.4% professional host presence — signaling a highly commercialized market.</li>
        <li><strong>Barcelona and Bangkok exhibit the highest professional host concentration</strong> (58-60% of supply), raising regulatory scrutiny concerns and suggesting mature, institutionalized short-term rental markets.</li>
        <li><strong>Paris and Sydney have no valid price data</strong> in this sample, limiting pricing comparisons — this data gap should be addressed before making market-entry decisions for those cities.</li>
        <li><strong>Rome shows the strongest guest demand</strong> with 1.77 avg reviews/month and the highest total review count (382,872), indicating robust booking activity despite moderate pricing.</li>
        <li><strong>Amsterdam has the lowest professional host share (6.8%)</strong>, suggesting a market dominated by individual hosts — potentially more vulnerable to regulatory changes affecting small operators.</li>
    </ol>
</div>

<section id="overview">
    <h2>1. Global Market Overview</h2>

    <div class="kpi-grid">
        <div class="kpi-card highlight">
            <div class="value">50,000</div>
            <div class="label">Total Listings</div>
        </div>
        <div class="kpi-card">
            <div class="value">7</div>
            <div class="label">Cities Analyzed</div>
        </div>
        <div class="kpi-card">
            <div class="value">74%</div>
            <div class="label">Entire Home/Apt</div>
        </div>
        <div class="kpi-card">
            <div class="value">48.2%</div>
            <div class="label">Price Data Missing</div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <h3>Listing Distribution by City</h3>
    <div class="chart-container">
        <div class="chart-title">Total Listings per City</div>
        <canvas id="listingsChart"></canvas>
    </div>

    <h3>Room-Type Composition by City</h3>
    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>City</th>
                <th>Entire Home/Apt</th>
                <th>Private Room</th>
                <th>Hotel Room</th>
                <th>Shared Room</th>
                <th>Entire Home Share</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td>London</td><td>7,343</td><td>3,411</td><td>14</td><td>32</td><td>44.0%</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Paris</td><td>12,288</td><td>1,490</td><td>125</td><td>24</td><td>88.2%</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Rome</td><td>4,387</td><td>1,284</td><td>40</td><td>13</td><td>68.7%</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Bangkok</td><td>2,858</td><td>1,087</td><td>27</td><td>46</td><td>57.6%</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Barcelona</td><td>1,769</td><td>769</td><td>4</td><td>16</td><td>54.1%</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Sydney</td><td>2,379</td><td>611</td><td>17</td><td>6</td><td>79.0%</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Amsterdam</td><td>774</td><td>201</td><td>8</td><td>4</td><td>43.7%</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</section>

<section id="pricing">
    <h2>2. Pricing Dynamics Across Cities</h2>

    <div class="data-note">
        <strong>Data Limitation:</strong> Paris (13,927 listings) and Sydney (3,013 listings) have no valid price data in this sample. Price comparisons are limited to 5 cities.
    </div>

    <h3>Median Nightly Price by City (USD)</h3>
    <div class="chart-container">
        <div class="chart-title">Median Price Comparison — Cities with Valid Price Data</div>
        <canvas id="medianPriceChart"></canvas>
    </div>

    <h3>Average Nightly Price by City and Room Type (USD)</h3>
    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>City</th>
                <th>Entire Home/Apt</th>
                <th>Private Room</th>
                <th>Shared Room</th>
                <th>Hotel Room</th>
                <th>City Median</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr class="price-high"><td>Bangkok</td><td>$1,500</td><td>$1,087</td><td>$388</td><td>$1,241</td><td><strong>$1,400</strong></td></tr>
            <tr class="price-mid"><td>Amsterdam</td><td>$250</td><td>$141</td><td>$74</td><td>$160</td><td><strong>$222</strong></td></tr>
            <tr class="price-low"><td>London</td><td>$176</td><td>$61</td><td>$30</td><td>$246</td><td><strong>$135</strong></td></tr>
            <tr class="price-low"><td>Barcelona</td><td>$167</td><td>$60</td><td>$43</td><td>$192</td><td><strong>$132</strong></td></tr>
            <tr class="price-low"><td>Rome</td><td>$140</td><td>$104</td><td>$50</td><td>$122</td><td><strong>$131</strong></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Paris</td><td colspan="4" style="text-align:center;color:#6b7280;">No price data available</td><td>—</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Sydney</td><td colspan="4" style="text-align:center;color:#6b7280;">No price data available</td><td>—</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>Price Dispersion Analysis</h3>
    <p>Among cities with available price data, Bangkok exhibits extreme price dispersion with a mean price ($2,337) nearly double its median ($1,500), indicating a long tail of ultra-premium listings. Amsterdam and London show more moderate dispersion ratios, suggesting a more balanced market distribution.</p>
</section>

<section id="supply">
    <h2>3. Supply Structure & Host Concentration</h2>

    <h3>Professional Host Share (Hosts with 5+ Listings)</h3>
    <div class="chart-container">
        <div class="chart-title">Percentage of Listings from Multi-Listing Hosts</div>
        <canvas id="profHostChart"></canvas>
    </div>

