    <p>Despite Bangkok's premium pricing, it ranks lowest in reviews-per-month, suggesting price sensitivity at that price point. Rome leads in demand intensity with 1.77 reviews/month despite mid-range pricing ($131 median), indicating strong value proposition. London's high absolute review volume (96,392 LTM) but moderate per-listing rate suggests a large but competitive market.</p>
</section>

<section id="availability">
    <h2>5. Availability & Booking Constraints</h2>

    <h3>Average Availability (Days per Year)</h3>
    <div class="chart-container">
        <div class="chart-title">Average Listing Availability (Days/Year)</div>
        <canvas id="availabilityChart"></canvas>
    </div>

    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>City</th>
                <th>Avg Availability</th>
                <th>Avg Minimum Nights</th>
                <th>Listings 30+ Min Nights</th>
                <th>Signal</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
